# Reverse-engineering scratch: the interceptor and standalone decoder that
# produced the protocol map, plus the raw payloads they captured. Superseded by
# nep2mqtt/ and kept out of the repo on purpose - two copies of a binary parser
# is one copy too many. The packets worth keeping live in tests/fixtures/.
capture/

# Raw captured frames, from anywhere. A frame carries the inverter's serial
# number, which is how the vendor cloud identifies the device - closer to a weak
# credential than to telemetry. tests/fixtures/ holds anonymised frames with
# synthetic serials and recomputed checksums; see the note in README. Nothing
# straight off the wire belongs in git.
raw/
*.pcap
*.pcapng


